  "_comment": "Phase-3b: a knight posed with a SKELETON of form bones. Each bone is a shaded solid that declares its own anchors; a child pins its pivot to a parent's world anchor via `attach`, so the parts meet no matter how the chest leans or a limb swings \u2014 connection is structural, not lucky. This is what lets the pose be steep (sword arm cocked high, torso leaning, legs in a stride) and still pass `connected`/`on_canvas`. Compare the hand-placed knight-forms-hero, which had to stay timid to avoid drifting apart.",
